From 4a04ffc7c070d881caeabc32f4f07d3c50251779 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:17:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): no large blurred shadows on the settings cards: the
 page scrolled at 17 fps

The settings page's cards had `shadow-lg` and `backdrop-blur-sm`, the
expanded method card `shadow-md`; the face card is thousands of pixels
tall, and WebKitGTK paints such shadows again on every scroll step.
Measured on a Snapdragon X laptop (WebKitGTK 2.50, its GL on Mesa's
zink, WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1 as it needs there) with the page
in a WebKitGTK view in a nested KWin: 17.5 frames a second while
scrolling and 16 % of a core at rest with them, 60 (16 ms frames) and
4 % without. A plain page scrolled at 60 either way, and neither the
DMA-BUF renderer, compositing nor Skia's CPU rendering changed it. The
cards keep their border and background; small shadows (buttons,
inputs) and the rings stay.
---
 app/src/app/configuration/-components/KeyringCard.tsx    | 2 +-
 app/src/app/configuration/-components/LockoutCard.tsx    | 2 +-
 app/src/app/configuration/-components/MethodCard.tsx     | 2 +-
 app/src/app/configuration/-components/MethodConfig.tsx   | 2 +-
 app/src/app/configuration/-components/StrategyConfig.tsx | 2 +-
 5 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

